GRUB's EFI init cancels the UEFI watchdog that the firmware's boot
manager - on Jetson, L4TLauncher, which arms it for 5 minutes before
starting GRUB - set up. On a board that depends on a reset to fall back to
the other A/B rootfs slot, that turns any hang inside GRUB (a bad config, a
wedged disk read) into a hang that only a power cycle ends. Re-arm it for
300 s instead. The kernel's EFI stub disarms it at ExitBootServices, as the
UEFI spec requires, and the boat's grub.cfg has no menu, so it can never
time out on someone reading the screen.

See docs/plans/ab-os-updates.md sections 5.1 and 5.5.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [A/B integration policy - upstream disables
the watchdog on purpose, for interactive menus]

--- a/grub-core/kern/efi/init.c
+++ b/grub-core/kern/efi/init.c
@@ -105,8 +105,17 @@
       grub_shim_lock_verifier_setup ();
     }
 
+  /*
+   * Re-arm the UEFI watchdog (300 s) instead of disabling it. The firmware's
+   * boot manager - on Jetson, L4TLauncher - arms it before starting this
+   * image, and a GRUB that hangs (a bad config, a wedged disk read) must
+   * still end in a reset so an A/B slot fallback can happen on the next
+   * boot. The kernel's EFI stub disarms it at ExitBootServices, as the UEFI
+   * spec requires, and a boot without a menu never waits on a human long
+   * enough to trip it.
+   */
   efi_call_4 (grub_efi_system_table->boot_services->set_watchdog_timer,
-	      0, 0, 0, NULL);
+	      300, 0x10000, 0, NULL);
 
   grub_efidisk_init ();
 }
